For production where you want the smallest fastest binaries:

Let's start with only -Os -fwrapv -fomit-frame-pointer -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables, which are very safe. 
Separately add -Wl,--gc-sections -fwhole-program -s -Wl,--build-id=none _only_ to the very last gcc step which links everything together. 
(If you added that to intermediary steps, things would fall apart and not work.)
--ONLY if grep -rnwe throw -e catch shows you use no exceptions, add -fno-exceptions
XXONLY if grep -rnwe dynamic_cast -e virtual shows you use no virtual methods or dynamic_cast, add -fno-rtti
XXONLY if grep -rnwe errno -e virtual shows you don't use errno, add -fno-math-errno
ONLY if grep -rnwe std: shows you don't use dynamic standard library methods (macro-like std such as std::max are fine to use), add -nodefaultlibs -lc -lgcc_s

XX-s -R .comment -R .gnu.version. It can be combined with --strip-unneeded to rem
XX-s -R .comment -R .gnu.version -Wl,--strip-unneeded

-fno-ident -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables 
-nostdlib and -ffreestanding

